#!RuleTest
#test FDA-SD9719 expect=skipped domain=DS
#note "The owner-ruled Domains.Exclude [DS] (absent-column-exceptions.tsv, 'M3 sister scope'): SDTMIG 3.4 defines none of DSENDTC/DSENRF/DSENRTPT/DSDUR in DS - a disposition event has a start and no end - and neither DSOCCUR nor DSSTAT, so all six conjuncts are structurally true and without the exclusion this sister would fire once per DS dataset on EVERY submission, with nothing a sponsor submits able to change it. The dataset is violating-shaped to prove ONLY the exclusion silences. The FDA arm needs the entry itself; the PMDA arm inherits DS from its parent's exclusion list."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
dataset DS class=EVENTS label="Disposition"
col STUDYID type=Char label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col DSSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col DSTERM  type=Char label="Reported Term for the Disposition Event"
col DSDECOD type=Char label="Standardized Disposition Term"
---
S1 | DS | 001 | 1 | COMPLETED | COMPLETED
